  "source": {
    "post_stream": {
      "posts": [
        {
          "id": 1933741,
          "username": "B2C-YYC",
          "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.shopify.com/b2c-yyc/{size}/235324_2.png",
          "created_at": "2026-11-06T17:20:04.213Z",
          "cooked": "<p><strong>Documentation request: Flow template deep links</strong></p>\n<p>The Flow template reference says templates with <code>discoverable = false</code> are accessible through a deep link, but doesn’t explain how to obtain or construct that link. My app has discoverable templates, and I want to link one of them through the app’s main screen. The documentation does not indicate how to structure the deep link to a Flow template, and whether the link will change if a revision is done to the template in the app extension, or if a new version of the app (without template changes) is deployed.</p>\n<p>Please document:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The supported URL format.</li>\n<li>How an app retrieves the published template ID, which differs from the extension’s TOML <code>uid</code>.</li>\n<li>Whether that ID remains stable after template updates, resubmissions, and app deployments.</li>\n<li>How to obtain a link for a non-discoverable template.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Is there a supported API or handle-based URL for this?</p>",
          "post_number": 1,
          "post_type": 1,
          "posts_count": 4,
          "updated_at": "2026-11-06T17:20:04.213Z",
          "reply_count": 0,
          "reply_to_post_number": null,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "incoming_link_count": 1,
