        {
          "id": 1935218,
          "username": "AndyX",
          "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.shopify.com/andyx/{size}/417600_2.png",
          "created_at": "2026-11-09T02:00:25.415Z",
          "cooked": "<p>For the discoverable templates you already have, there is a manual way to get the link: open the published template in Flow’s template library and use its Share button, rather than building a URL from the TOML uid. In this developer-forum thread, paul_n points to Share and explains that library previews don’t work during development; the template needs to be published first:</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox discoursetopic\" data-onebox-src=\"https://community.shopify.dev/t/how-to-deep-link-to-a-flow-template/33380\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n      <img src=\"https://canada1.discourse-cdn.com/shopifyforum/original/4X/8/1/8/8185926241fa3aa1bc3a2ca5f82e6c0812dce5ca.png\" class=\"site-icon\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"3E972F\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://community.shopify.dev/t/how-to-deep-link-to-a-flow-template/33380\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\" title=\"06:16PM - 16 April 2026\">Shopify Developer Community Forums – 16 Apr 26</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    <div class=\"aspect-image\" style=\"--aspect-ratio:690/362;\"><img src=\"https://canada1.discourse-cdn.com/shopifyforum/optimized/4X/6/2/6/6263175c147451c38b49d33bcbc04a37a89a0b1b_2_690x362.jpeg\" class=\"thumbnail\" alt=\"\" width=\"690\" height=\"362\" data-dominant-color=\"8ACBC4\"></div>\n\n<div class=\"title-wrapper\">\n  <h3><a href=\"https://community.shopify.dev/t/how-to-deep-link-to-a-flow-template/33380\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">How to deep link to a Flow template?</a></h3>\n  <div class=\"topic-category\">\n      <span class=\"badge-wrapper bullet\">\n        <span class=\"badge-category-bg\" style=\"background-color: #B3B5B4;\"></span>\n        <span class=\"badge-category clear-badge\">\n          <span class=\"category-name\">Shopify Flow</span>\n        </span>\n      </span>\n    <div class=\"topic-header-extra\">\n      <div class=\"list-tags\">\n        <div class=\"discourse-tags\">\n          <svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-tag svg-icon svg-string\"><use href=\"#tag\"></use></svg>\n            <span class=\"discourse-tag simple\">templates</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n  <p>We’re currently trying to link to a flow template inside our embedded app.  That would make the process faster and less confusing, compared to having to scroll the template list.  We also can’t guess the link because we’re not able to preview our...</p>\n\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n\n<p>That gives you a link to use from your app, but it doesn’t answer your automation and stability questions. That thread doesn’t document an API for retrieving the ID, guarantee that the link survives revisions, or explain how to obtain it for a non-discoverable template. I wouldn’t infer those guarantees from the Share link.</p>",
