        {
          "id": 1935245,
          "username": "faisaltech",
          "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/f/b77776/{size}.png",
          "created_at": "2026-11-09T05:47:01.147Z",
          "cooked": "<p>Thanks for sharing that manual workaround, AndyX — publishing the template and copying the Share link is a useful stopgap for discoverable templates. I agree the bigger gap is still stability and automation, especially whether that ID survives updates and redeploys. It would help a lot if Shopify documented the supported format and a way to retrieve the ID for non-discoverable templates, so apps do not have to rely on guessing or manual steps.</p>",
