    "ai_summary": {
      "id": 1876516,
      "summarized_text": "The discussion concerns how apps can deep-link to Flow templates, particularly how to obtain the published template ID and whether links remain valid after template or app updates. The documentation reportedly says non-discoverable templates can be opened through a deep link, but does not specify the URL format or how to retrieve that link.\n\nA suggested workaround for discoverable templates is to publish the template, open it in Flow’s template library, and copy the URL using the Share button. This does not provide an automated method or establish that the link remains stable through revisions, resubmissions, or app deployments. The extension’s TOML `uid` is also not the same as the published template ID.\n\nParticipants request documentation of the supported link format, ID retrieval, link stability, and a method for non-discoverable templates. No supported API or stability guarantees are identified, so the main questions remain unresolved.",
      "algorithm": "gpt-6-luna",
