  "comments": [
    {
      "author": "AndyX",
      "text": "For the discoverable templates you already have, there is a manual way to get the link: open the published template in Flow’s template library and use its Share button, rather than building a URL from the TOML uid. In this developer-forum thread, paul_n points to Share and explains that library previews don’t work during development; the template needs to be published first: \n \n   \n       \n\n       Shopify Developer Community Forums – 16 Apr 26 \n   \n\n   \n       \n\n \n    How to deep link to a Flow template?  \n   \n       \n          \n         \n           Shopify Flow \n         \n       \n     \n       \n         \n              \n             templates \n         \n       \n     \n   \n \n\n   We’re currently trying to link to a flow template inside our embedded app.  That would make the process faster and less confusing, compared to having to scroll the template list.  We also can’t guess the link because we’re not able to preview our... \n\n\n   \n\n   \n    \n    \n   \n\n    \n \n\n That gives you a link to use from your app, but it doesn’t answer your automation and stability questions. That thread doesn’t document an API for retrieving the ID, guarantee that the link survives revisions, or explain how to obtain it for a non-discoverable template. I wouldn’t infer those guarantees from the Share link.",
      "at": "2026-11-09T02:00:25.415Z",
      "url": "https://community.shopify.com/t/how-to-deep-link-to-flow-templates-from-their-source-apps/711311/2"
    },
    {
      "author": "B2C-YYC",
      "text": "Thanks for referencing the previous thread,  @AndyX  \nI will tag  @paul_n  for comment (hopefully) re: my questions about stability of the links as versions are deployed. TIA",
      "at": "2026-11-09T04:30:09.601Z",
      "url": "https://community.shopify.com/t/how-to-deep-link-to-flow-templates-from-their-source-apps/711311/3"
    },
    {
      "author": "faisaltech",
      "text": "Thanks for sharing that manual workaround, AndyX — publishing the template and copying the Share link is a useful stopgap for discoverable templates. I agree the bigger gap is still stability and automation, especially whether that ID survives updates and redeploys. It would help a lot if Shopify documented the supported format and a way to retrieve the ID for non-discoverable templates, so apps do not have to rely on guessing or manual steps.",
      "at": "2026-11-09T05:47:01.147Z",
      "url": "https://community.shopify.com/t/how-to-deep-link-to-flow-templates-from-their-source-apps/711311/4"
    }
  ],
